ithmic functional behavior for a proposed drainon?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:c6017b46203056215fb86d1767013fdd70417bf1f8ef68b01c482ffe259bdfae","title":"Can inflationary observations restrict how far dark energy departs from a cosmological constant when common swampland parameters govern both sectors? A related question is whether a small total inflaton excursion still permits observable primordial tensors.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0035"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:c62882ff6fae06f50b5f7c46611fa124b1390d0e4077a2bdc31c3b8970661a1b","title":"Can varying the shape scale of a supergravity-inspired plateau maintain observational agreement while bringing the conjecture parameters toward order unity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:c63db150c20841fc16ad24758427ee0c2957be51664d5368191c9f6c3ea03263","title":"Can the complete light spectrum reproduce the prepotential terms responsible for infinite distance, and can K-point BPS states be organized into a concrete higher-genus counting problem?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:c624961b7416c3514d15baa7794a78bc21edf26ea672030440ff3e1ef13e0a6f","title":"Can a simple stabilized modulus with Planck-suppressed interactions satisfy the proposed scalar bound?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:c6f74996719d60dc1ce3b175340d1a5fe6ff090633a62c1824b7aaafcbf6d8d6","title":"Can a renormalizable R-symmetric Wess–Zumino model with generic coefficients possess an R-breaking supersymmetric vacuum despite having more R-charge-2 fields than R-charge-0 fields, and what does that imply f